#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>General Setup</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>General</guilabel> configuration dialog allows you to define "
"some basic &kdevelop; behaviour which seldom will change in everyday work. "
"This concerns:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "General project options such as"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"defining a <link linkend=\"setup-main-projects\">default parent directory</"
"link> &kdevelop; shall use for new projects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"deciding whether you want &kdevelop; to <link linkend=\"setup-main-preload"
"\">automatically load</link> the project you last worked on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selecting a font for the most commonly used output view windows, namely:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the <link linkend=\"setup-main-messages-font\">Messages Output View</link> "
"&kdevelop; uses to communicate &eg; compilation progresses, and"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the <link linkend=\"setup-main-applications-font\">Application Output View</"
"link> which will show error and state information concerning a running "
"application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some common behaviour concerning the displayed lines in the "
"<guilabel>Messages Output View</guilabel> window, namely:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"whether long lines will <link linkend=\"setup-main-wrap\">wrap around</"
"link>, and"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"if <link linkend=\"setup-main-navigation\">directory entry and exit "
"messages</link> issued by <command>make</command> will be shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <link linkend=\"setup-main-compile\">level of detail</link> of messages "
"concerning the compilation process shown in the <guilabel>Messages Output "
"View</guilabel> window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "The general configuration dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Load last project on startup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mark this checkbox if you want to continue to work with the last project you "
"worked on. This will cause &kdevelop; to automatically load this project on "
"start-up. It will usually be shown in the state you left work so you can "
"readily proceed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default projects directory:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kdevelop; uses a common parent directory for all new projects. "
"Enter the absolute path of this common directory in the box or select it "
"from your directory structure. &kdevelop; will place the any new project "
"here as a subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may of course change the directory path of a new project at the time you "
"set it up in the <link linkend=\"applicationwizard\">&appwizard;</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "Window font:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select a font suitable for the <guilabel>Messages Output View</guilabel> "
"window click the <guilabel>Window Font</guilabel> button showing the "
"currently selected font (it says <quote>Luxi Sans</quote> in the above "
"illustration). The &kde; standard <guilabel>Select Font</guilabel> dialog "
"will pop up from which you may select the font to be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On first start-up, &kdevelop; initializes this font setting to the standard "
"font for which your &kde; user has been configured. <emphasis>This setting "
"is fixed</emphasis>, so if you alter <menuchoice><guimenuitem>Preferences</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Appearances &amp; Themes</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Fonts</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the "
"<guilabel>Control Center</guilabel>, this will not effect this &kdevelop; "
"font selection. You will have to explicitely reselect the <guilabel>Messages "
"Output View</guilabel> window font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "Line wrapping"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kdevelop; will wrap long lines around in the <guilabel>Messages "
"Output View</guilabel> window so that valuable information will not be "
"easily overlooked. In some cases this will clutter long message lists. "
"Remove the checkbox mark if you do not want the lines wrap around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is an alternative way to switch the line wrapping. Just &RMB; click in "
"the <guilabel>Messages Output View</guilabel> window and mark/unmark the "
"<guimenuitem>Line Wrapping</guimenuitem> entry in the menu which will pop up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory navigation messages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <command>make</command> tool usually will display messages like "
"<quote>Entering directory</quote>, or <quote>Leaving directory</quote> when "
"it switches the directories it currently works in. As this clutters the "
"messages list in the <guilabel>Messages Output View</guilabel> window, "
"&kdevelop; suppresses those messages by default. Mark the checkbox if you "
"want to protocol which directories <command>make</command> worked in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changes in this setting effect the processing of new messages only. Old "
"directory navigation messages will be kept visible when you switch this "
"feature off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Compiler Output"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; preprocesses the messages the <guilabel>Messages Output View</"
"guilabel> window receives during the build processes in order to filter "
"superfluous information. You can control the level of detail &kdevelop; will "
"display using the radio buttons in this field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Very Short"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displays only warnings, errors, and the filenames which are compiled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Short"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suppresses all compiler flags and formats the output to be more readable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full"
msgstr "Complet"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displays all output messages unmodified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is an alternative way to switch the compiler output detail. Just right "
"click in the <guilabel>Messages Output View</guilabel> window and select the "
"according detail level from the popup menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Application Output View</guilabel> <guilabel>Window font:</"
"guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Application Output View</guilabel> window is used to display "
"error and state information from applications which are run from inside "
"&kdevelop;. These are informations the applications usually sends to the "
"console when run stand-alone. So you do not need to leave the IDE when "
"testing the application you currently work on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select a font suitable for the <guilabel>Application Output View</"
"guilabel> window click the <guilabel>Window Font</guilabel> button showing "
"the currently selected font (it says <quote>Luxi Sans</quote> in the above "
"illustration). The &kde; standard <guilabel>Select Font</guilabel> dialog "
"will pop up from which you may select the font to be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On first start-up, &kdevelop; initializes this font setting to the standard "
"font for which your &kde; user has been configured. <emphasis>This setting "
"is fixed</emphasis>, so if you alter <menuchoice><guimenuitem>Preferences</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Appearances &amp; Themes</"
"guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Fonts</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the "
"<guilabel>Control Center</guilabel>, this will not effect this &kdevelop; "
"font selection. You will have to explicitely reselect the "
"<guilabel>Application Output View</guilabel> window font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Selecting the User Interface</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: setup.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "user interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: secondary
#: setup.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "switch modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: setup.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "switch UI modes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As already said in the <link linkend=\"uimodes-survey\">Available User "
"Interface Modes</link> chapter there are four different ways the &kdevelop; "
"work area may be set up, namely:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:289
#, no-c-format
msgid "IDEAl Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Child Frame Windows Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tabbed Pages Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:298
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toplevel Windows Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To switch the user interface mode select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure KDevelop...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from "
"the menus. The <guilabel>Customize KDevelop</guilabel> dialog will pop up, "
"where you have to select <guilabel>User Interface</guilabel> in the left "
"hand tree. This will display the following settings dialog to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Select a user interface mode</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:311
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Select a user interface mode</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the radio button of the user interface mode you want to switch to, "
"then click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not forget to restart &kdevelop; in order to let any of these selections "
"take effect."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you selected either the <guilabel>IDEAl window mode</guilabel> or the "
"<guilabel>Tabbed pages mode</guilabel> two more configuration sections will "
"become available: <link linkend=\"setup-ui-tabs\">Use Tabs</link> and <link "
"linkend=\"setup-ui-hover\">Use Close On Hover</link>. These allow to "
"configure under which circumstances tabs will be shown on top of the "
"document windows and whether you may close the document by a click on the "
"tab icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In <guilabel>IDEAl window mode</guilabel> only yet another configuration "
"section will be available, <link linkend=\"setup-ui-toolview\">Toolview Tab "
"Layout</link> which effectively allows to select between different sizes of "
"the toolview tabs which surround the main working area in this mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the Documents Tab Bar Display"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the IDEAl and tabbed pages modes there will be named tabs on top of the "
"document windows by default, so you can easily select different documents "
"with a &LMB; click. If you prefer to provide more space for the document "
"windows in the &kdevelop; main work area, you may change to another "
"behaviour in the <guilabel>Use Tabs</guilabel> configuration section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always"
msgstr "Totjorn"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the default &mdash; show a tab comprising an icon and the document "
"name on top of any document window in the &kdevelop; main area display."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "When more than one"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not show a tab when only one document is displayed. If there is more than "
"one document, however, &kdevelop; will display an according tab bar as in "
"the <guilabel>Always</guilabel> selection above. You may want to select this "
"mode if you work on a single document most of the time as this provides more "
"vertical space."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "Never"
msgstr "Jamai"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Never show any document selection tab. You may prefer this mode if you "
"seldom use the mouse to switch between documents. It provides more vertical "
"space for all document windows. To select another the document window or to "
"close any, use the &kdevelop; <guimenu>Window</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting Up to Close a Document by a Click On Its Tab"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:368
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you configured &kdevelop; to display the documents tab bar, either "
"always or when more than one document is displayed in the main work area, "
"you may add more functionality to the tabs beyond their document selection "
"capability. Use the <guilabel>Use Close On Hover</guilabel> coniguration "
"section for this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>No</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is standard behaviour. No extra functionality is added to the tabs. "
"They may be used only to select document windows on &LMB; clicks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Yes</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you selected this radio button, &kdevelop; will allow to close a "
"document window by a &LMB; click. Use the mouse to point at the small icon "
"on the on the left tab border. It will change to a close symbol. Now click "
"with the &LMB; on this changed symbol and &kdevelop; will close the "
"according document window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "Yes, Delayed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After selecting this radio button, &kdevelop; will allow to close a document "
"window as shown in the <guilabel>Yes</guilabel> case above. The icon will "
"not change instantly, however, but there will be a short delay before the "
"close icon shows up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:396
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the Toolview Tab Layout"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Toolview Tab Layout</guilabel> configuration section will be "
"available in IDEAl mode only. Use these radio buttons to set up the look of "
"the toolview tabs which surround the main working area in this mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icons"
msgstr "Icònas"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each tab will show an icon only. If the associated toolview is displayed, "
"the tab will open and a descriptive text for this toolview be shown. You may "
"want to use this mode if you work on a monitor with limited resolution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The icons are not very descriptive, however. If you want to find out which "
"toolview is assigned to a given tab, point at it with the mouse and wait a "
"second. A short tooltip will then pop up with the toolview name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text"
msgstr "Tèxt"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the default toolview tab display mode. Each tab displays the name of "
"its associated toolwiew."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text and Icons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the standard text toolview display looks too flat to you and you are "
"working on a high-resolution monitor you may want to select this radio "
"button. It will cause the name of the associated toolview be displayed on "
"each tab plus an icon to the left of it, making the tabs easier to "
"distinguish. See the <link linkend=\"folded-toolview-tabs\">Folded Toolview "
"Tabs</link> illustration below for an example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:431
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folded Toolview Tabs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:433
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you selected the IDEAl mode toolview tabs to display texts (with or "
"without accompanying icons) you need not worry about them being hidden "
"behind some toolview window. If one of the bottom toolview windows occupies "
"more space than is available to display all (vertical) tabs, they will fold "
"around as this illustration shows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:442
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<phrase>Toolview tabs fold to not be hidden behind another view window</"
"phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Toolview tabs fold to not be hidden behind another view window</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The active toolview window must be shown fixed (non-overlap mode), sharing "
"the work area with the other windows, to force such tab folding. Press the "
"small square in the window border to accomplish this as shown in the example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Selecting an Editor</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; allows you to select your favorite text editor tool. Mark the "
"<guilabel>Editor</guilabel> entry in the left hand side selections tree of "
"the <guilabel>Configure KDevelop</guilabel> window. The following dialog "
"will be displayed to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Select an editor</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Select an editor</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To select a new editor, click on the arrow on the drop down list field. "
"Depending on the editor parts interfaces your &kde; version has compiled in "
"you will be provided with a list of editors you may select from (see the "
"<link linkend=\"setup-editor-kparts\">Important</link> note below for this). "
"Click on the editor of your liking and click <guilabel>OK</guilabel>. "
"Currently there are tree possibilities:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid "Embedded Advanced Text Editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is the &kde; standard <application>Kate</application> editor part."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid "Embedded Vim Component"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This provides the look and feel of the base &Linux; <application>vi</"
"application> editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You need to have a suitable <application>Vim</application> application "
"installed. Have a look at the <ulink url=\"http://www.freehackers.org/kvim/"
"\">KVim</ulink> website for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Furthermore you need to configure the KParts Vim component in the "
"<guilabel>&kde; Control Center</guilabel> (<menuchoice><guimenuitem>KDE "
"Components</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Vim Component Configuration</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>) before you can use it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "Qt Designer Based Text Editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the editor &Qt; provides in its <application>Designer</application> "
"component."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These editor interfaces are fully integrated in the &kdevelop; IDE concept. "
"Particularly the possibility to jump to the offending source code line by "
"just clicking on an error message in the <guilabel>Messages Output View</"
"guilabel> window has been provided."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changing the editor will not effect already open files. There are two "
"possibilities to proceed. Either close all open text windows and reopen them "
"one by one. Or simply close the whole project and reopen it again. The "
"windows will then automatically open under the new text editor interface."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:519
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"KDevelop lets you use editor interfaces which have registered with &kde; and "
"that provide a KatePart interface. If you miss one one of the selections "
"shown above check your &kde; installation if the corresponding KPart was "
"correctly installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:525
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Selecting a Source Format Style</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; automatically formats a source text in a predefined style. This "
"style is highly configurable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The reformat source feature is currently available for C, C++, and &Java; "
"only. Especially you cannot use it for scripting languages like &eg; PHP. "
"This is because &kdevelop; uses the <ulink url=\"http://astyle.sourceforge."
"net/\">astyle</ulink> application to implement this feature."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To set up a specific format style, select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure KDevelop...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from "
"the menubar. The <guilabel>Customize KDevelop</guilabel> dialog will pop up, "
"where you have to select <guilabel>Source Formatter</guilabel> in the left "
"hand tree. This will display a series of three settings dialog tabs to the "
"right, namely a <link linkend=\"setup-format-general\">General Formatting "
"Setup</link>, a <link linkend=\"setup-format-indent\">Indentation Style "
"Setup</link>, and a <link linkend=\"setup-format-other\">Other Formatting "
"Setup</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any style changes apply to newly entered text only. If you want to change "
"the formatting style of an already existing source text you will have to "
"explicitely use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Reformat "
"Source</guimenuitem></menuchoice> command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The exact outcome of these style formatting definitions depends on the <link "
"linkend=\"setup-editor\">editor</link> you use. Currently, most settings are "
"tailored to the Kate editor part (the <quote>Embedded Advanced Text Editor</"
"quote>). Some other editors (&eg; the Qt editor) may rely on their own "
"configuration settings. You will have to experiment in this case to find out "
"the exact effects of the style settings provided here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There may be incompatibilities between the configuration style settings "
"provided here and the editor you use up to the extent that in extreme cases "
"it even might destroy your files. Make sure you have a backup of your source "
"files before you try out these settings with an none KDE standard editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Formatting Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab of the <guilabel>Source Formatter</"
"guilabel> dialog allows you to select one out of five predefined source "
"format styles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Source format style general setup</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Source format style general setup</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A formatted source example will be displayed in the field to the right. If "
"none of the predefined styles is to your liking, you may click the top "
"<guilabel>User defined</guilabel> radio button and define your own source "
"formatting style preferences on the other two tabs which will become "
"available then."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently only the predefined source formatting styles will be demonstrated "
"by an example text. If you decide to define your own style, no example "
"display will be available. You have to experiment on an actual source text "
"to tailor the settings to your liking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Style Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Proper indentation is the main means to enhance readability of a source "
"text. I you selected the <guilabel>Indentation</guilabel> tab of the "
"<guilabel>Source Formatter</guilabel> dialog you will be presented with a "
"series of indentation formatting choices grouped into three boxes as "
"following."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Source format indentation style setup</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Source format indentation style setup</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Settings"
msgstr "Paramètres per defaut"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The preset format choices will cause the source text to resemble the ANSI "
"formatting style:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: setup.docbook:606 setup.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"namespace foospace\n"
"{\n"
"  int Foo()\n"
"  {\n"
"    if (isBar)\n"
"    {\n"
"      bar();\n"
"      return 1;\n"
"    }\n"
"    else\n"
"      return 0;\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining Indentation Width and Characters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The radio buttons grouped in the <guilabel>Filling</guilabel> group define "
"how indents in the source text will be drawn."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use tabs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will cause the editor to insert a tab character for each indentation "
"level. The tab width is predefined in the editor settings (8 or 4 character "
"columns usually). Use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to "
"redefine it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The actual tab width definition procedure depends on the editor you selected "
"in the <link linkend=\"setup-editor\">Selecting an Editor</link> "
"configuration step. You will have to look up the corresponding editor help "
"to find out."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select this radio button, the editor will enter a number of spaces "
"for each indentation level. Change the number from the default 2 to the "
"indentation width you prefer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indented Entities"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This defines which of the (C/C++) entities will be formatted with an extra "
"indent beyond the current indentation level."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default only <guilabel>namespaces</guilabel> and <guilabel>labels</"
"guilabel> will be extra indented. You may want to experiment with various "
"settings to tailor those extra indents to your liking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid "Continuation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:656
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The settings grouped here apply to those cases where the source formatter "
"automatically wraps around long source lines. It takes two special cases in "
"account, namely that in deeply nested indents there should remain enough "
"room for the source and that conditionals should get extra indent levels on "
"continuation to make them stand out properly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This applies to <emphasis>static word wrap cases</emphasis> only where a "
"fixed maximum line width is used in the source text. If you set up your "
"editor to dynamically wrap around long lines in display only (which is "
"possible in the &kate; editor part) the effects of these settings usually "
"will not show."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid "Maximum in statement"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This setting limits the maximum possible indentation for the continuation "
"lines so that enough space will remain to keep the text readable. No "
"continuation line will ever be indented beyond the number of columns you "
"selected in this field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default is set to 40 character columns (half a standard 80 column page). "
"You may want to increase this value to account for wider paper (e.g if you "
"use landscape printing for your sources). Or decrease the value accordingly "
"to take larger margin settings of your printouts into account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum in conditional"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:679
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Conditionals or source following &eg; an assignment operator should usually "
"get an extra indent on continuation lines in order to keep the text "
"readable. The amount of this extra indent is defined here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default is set to <quote>Twice current</quote> which means that "
"continued conditionals will get an extra indent level of the standard "
"indentation size you selected in the <link linkend=\"setup-format-indent-"
"filling\">Filling</link> group. You may change this extra indent to another "
"fixed width (including zero) using the arrows or by entering the value "
"directly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:695
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other Formatting Setup"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:702
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Other source format style settings</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:703
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Other source format style settings</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling the position of braces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:713
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The radio buttons the (somewhat misnamed) <guilabel>Brackets</guilabel> "
"group control the position of block delimiting braces in a (C/C++) source "
"text. There are three possibilities from which you can select."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "Break"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This inserts a line break before each opening brace. Both delimiting braces "
"of any block will be put at the same indentation level as the block head "
"statement."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid "Attach"
msgstr "Jónher"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will keep the opening brace of a block in line with the block head "
"statement. Closing braces will be on the same indentation level as the block "
"head statement. The <token>else</token> of an <token>if</token> statement "
"will be kept in line with the closing brace of the preceding block."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: setup.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"namespace foospace {\n"
"  int Foo() {\n"
"    if (isBar) {\n"
"      bar();\n"
"      return 1;\n"
"    } else\n"
"      return 0;\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "Linux Style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:739
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a compromise of the above listed styles. Functional block delimiting "
"braces will be put on extra lines. Braces opening a block in a conditional "
"or loop statement will be kept in line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: setup.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"namespace foospace\n"
"{\n"
"  int Foo()\n"
"  {\n"
"    if (isBar) {\n"
"      bar();\n"
"      return 1;\n"
"    } else\n"
"      return 0;\n"
"  }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:750
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling Extra Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid "By default &kdevelop; does minimize the use of spaces in source texts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: setup.docbook:757
#, no-c-format
msgid "if (isBar(fooArg)==barValue)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may enhance readability if you force the source formatter to insert "
"extra spaces in special positions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:764
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add spaces around parentheses"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In fact what is meant is to add spaces around the text put in parentheses. "
"This enhances the readabilitiy of function arguments and conditionals."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: setup.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid "if ( isBar( fooArg )==barValue )"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:771
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add spaces around operators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:773
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will put spaces around assignment and comparison operators to enhance "
"the readability."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: setup.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid "if (isBar(fooArg) == barValue)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling the formatting of one-line constructs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:784
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a few cases where you don't want the source formatter to split a "
"long line apart. For C/C++ code this can be controlled here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:789
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep one-line statements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:790
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This keeps single line statements together in some situations even if they "
"exceed a fixed maximum line length."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:795
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep one-line blocks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This keeps single line blocks together in some situations even if they "
"exceed a fixed maximum line length."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:811
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Setting Up the Code Snippets Tool</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:813
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When editing in &kdevelop; you can store often used parts of code as <link "
"linkend=\"editing-snippets\">Code Snippets</link>. To configure the "
"capabilities of the code snippets part select <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure KDevelop...</guimenuitem> "
"</menuchoice> from the menubar. The <guilabel>Customize KDevelop</guilabel> "
"dialog will pop up, where you have to select <guilabel>Code Snippets</"
"guilabel> in the left hand tree. This will show the following dialog in the "
"right hand side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:822
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the code snippets tool"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:823
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the Code Snippets tool"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:831
#, no-c-format
msgid "Activate Snippet Preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:833
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mark the <guilabel>Show snippet's text in tooltip</guilabel> checkbox if you "
"want to view the stored text in a tooltip window whenever you keep the mouse "
"cursor over the title of that snippet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:840
#, no-c-format
msgid "Working with Snippet Variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:842
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Code Snippets</guilabel> tool allows for a variable text in "
"predefined places any time you insert a snippet into a file. To accomplish "
"this <guilabel>Code Snippets</guilabel> provides its own variables' "
"mechanism. You can set up its behaviour in the <guilabel>Variables</"
"guilabel> group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:850
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delimiter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:851
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Code Snippets</guilabel> tool distinguishes variables in the "
"text by surrounding the variable name with special delimiter symbols. To use "
"your own delimiter symbol, change the predefined <guilabel>$</guilabel> "
"character in the <guilabel>Delimiter</guilabel> field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:856
#, no-c-format
msgid "Input method for variables"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:858
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Single dialog for each variable within a snippet</guilabel> "
"&ndash; will in turn pop up a separate dialog for each variable which the "
"tool finds when inserting the selected code snippet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:861
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>One dialog for all variables within a snippet</guilabel> &ndash; "
"will pop up a common dialog where the user has to fill in the values of all "
"variables before the snippet will be inserted"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:874
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Configuring the File Selector</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:876
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; provides a <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> plugin which, when "
"loaded at start-up, allows to navigate to any file or directory in the "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:887
#, no-c-format
msgid "The file selector in IDEAl mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:888
#, no-c-format
msgid "The file selector (IDEAl mode)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The behaviour of the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> can be highly "
"configured. Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure KDevelop...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the "
"menubar. The <guilabel>Customize KDevelop</guilabel> dialog will pop up, "
"where you have to select <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> in the left hand "
"tree. This will show the following dialog in the right hand side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:907
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Configuring the file selector</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:908
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Configuring the file selector</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:916
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:918
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a toolbar on top of the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> which "
"can be configured as usual in the <guilabel>Toolbar</guilabel> group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:923
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add an Action to the Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select an item in the right hand <guilabel>Selected actions</guilabel> list "
"after which the new action should be inserted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the action to be inserted in the left hand <guilabel>Available "
"actions</guilabel> list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:935
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the right (upper) arrow between both lists."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:938
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The action will be removed from the <guilabel>Available actions</guilabel> "
"list and inserted into the <guilabel>Selected actions</guilabel> list below "
"the selected item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove an Action from the Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:946
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the item to be removed in the right hand <guilabel>Selected actions</"
"guilabel> list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:951
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the left (lower) arrow between both lists."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The selected item will be removed from the <guilabel>Selected actions</"
"guilabel> list and put back into the <guilabel>Available actions</guilabel> "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:960
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reorder the Actions on the Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:962
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the action to be moved in the right hand <guilabel>Selected actions</"
"guilabel> list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:967
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click the up or down arrow to the right of this list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The selected item will be moved up or down the <guilabel>Selected actions</"
"guilabel> list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid "Defining When the Contents Should Change"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Updating the contents in the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> window takes "
"time and resources, esp. when changing to another directory. Therefore "
"<guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> is set up by default in such a way that "
"its contents change only on demand, &ie; when you select another directory "
"or when you explicitely want to refresh its contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guilabel>Reload</guilabel> button in the toolbar to update the "
"contents of the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel>. This toolbar button is "
"not available by default, however. You must <link linkend=\"setup-"
"fileselector-add-action\">insert it there</link> first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:989
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can configure the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> to immediately "
"reflect certain changes in your work. The settings in the <guilabel>Auto "
"Synchronization</guilabel> group of the configuration dialog are responsible "
"for this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:995
#, no-c-format
msgid "When a document becomes active"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:996
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select this checkbox, the contents in the <guilabel>File Selector</"
"guilabel> window will be updated whenever you go to another already open "
"document, &eg; when you click on the tab of the according edit window in "
"IDEAl mode. If necessary the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> will switch "
"to the directory this file belongs to and update the display to show the "
"actual contents in there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid "When a document is opened"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1002
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select this checkbox, the contents in the <guilabel>File Selector</"
"guilabel> window will be updated whenever a document will be opened, &eg; by "
"the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> menu. If necessary the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> will "
"switch to the directory this file belongs to and update the display to show "
"the actual contents in there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid "When the file selector becomes visible"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1008
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select this checkbox, the contents in the <guilabel>File Selector</"
"guilabel> window will be updated whenever it gets visible again. If "
"necessary it will switch to the directory the actual document belongs to and "
"update the display to show the actual contents in there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1014
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may freely combine these settings to tailor the actualization behaviour "
"of the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> to your liking."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:1021
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling the History in the Comboboxes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1023
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two comboboxes on top and bottom of the <guilabel>File Selector</"
"guilabel> contents window which control the directory to be displayed (top "
"combobox) and the filters to be applied to the file display (bottom "
"combobox). A history of the most recent settings is kept in the selection "
"field of each combobox. You can configure the number of history entries as "
"follows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1032
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remember locations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1033
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter here the maximum number of directory selections the upper combobox "
"shall remember."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1038
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remember filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1039
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter here the maximum number of filter definitions the lower combobox shall "
"remember."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:1045
#, no-c-format
msgid "Controlling What Should be Remembered Between Sessions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1047
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default the <guilabel>File Selector</guilabel> is set up so that it shows "
"the display of the most recent session again at the next &kdevelop; start-"
"up. You may change this behaviour in the <guilabel>Session</guilabel> "
"configuration group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1051
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &kdevelop; was automatically restarted by the &kde; session manager the "
"changes in these settings will have no effect. In this case location and "
"filter settings of the most recent &kde; session will always be restored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore location"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1060
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remove the checkbox mark here if you don't want the displayed location be "
"remembered between sessions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1063
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you selected one of the <link linkend=\"setup-fileselector-autosync"
"\">automatic update</link> settings the displayed location might "
"automatically change regardless what has been remembered from the recent "
"session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1069
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restore filters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1071
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remove the checkbox mark here if you don't want the filters applied to the "
"display be remembered between sessions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1084
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the New File Wizard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1086 setup.docbook:1730 setup.docbook:1750 setup.docbook:1763
#: setup.docbook:1770 setup.docbook:1778 setup.docbook:1786 setup.docbook:1795
#: setup.docbook:1802 setup.docbook:1810 setup.docbook:1818
#, no-c-format
msgid "(... to be written ...)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1097
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring the Documentation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1099
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; contains a very powerful documentation facility which provides "
"access to several kinds of extensive documentation. In &eg; IDEAl mode you "
"find a <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> tab at the right border of the "
"work area."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:1108
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kdevelop; documentation window in IDEAl mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1109
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kdevelop; documentation window (IDEAl mode)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; must have loaded the <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> plugin in "
"order to view the documentation tree. See the <link linkend=\"setup-plugins"
"\">Plugin Tools</link> section for more info."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may set up contents and behaviour of the various parts of this "
"documentation window if you select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure KDevelop...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the "
"menubar. The <guilabel>Customize KDevelop</guilabel> dialog will pop up, "
"where you have to select <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> in the left hand "
"window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The thus displayed <link linkend=\"configure-docu-general\">configuration "
"page</link> shows three tabbed configuration dialog pages, namely:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1128
#, no-c-format
msgid "Documentation Collections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full Text Search"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other"
msgstr "Autre"

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting Up Documentation Collections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The documentation configuration settings have been divided into a series of "
"documentation collections, each providing access to documentation files of "
"some unique format and content type. These setups control which "
"documentation items will be listed on the <guilabel>Contents</guilabel> page "
"of the &kdevelop; <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> facility, and how the "
"user may access documentation details by indexed and full text searches."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> tab provides a series of "
"configuration pages which are ordered vertically like a stack of index "
"cards. One page at a time will open after a click on its index card title:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1143
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Qt; Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1144
#, no-c-format
msgid "CHM Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Doxygen Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1146
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdevelop; TOC Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Devhelp Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: setup.docbook:1148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:1157
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Setting up documentation collections</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1158
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Setting up documentation collections</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1166
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common Documentation Setup Structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All configurations pages on the <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> tab use a "
"common layout. You will find the currently available documentation items of "
"this type listed on the open page to the left and a set of buttons to the "
"right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:1174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Buttons to Maintain Documentation List Contents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three buttons available to maintain the contents of the "
"documentation setup pages:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: setup.docbook:1182
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Add</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a <guilabel>Documentation Catalog Properties</guilabel> dialog as "
"shown below where you can select the source location of the documentation "
"item to be added and name it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: setup.docbook:1188
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit"
msgstr "Edicion"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a <guilabel>Documentation Catalog Properties</guilabel> dialog as "
"shown below where you can change the source location of the documentation "
"item previously selected in the list and rename it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: setup.docbook:1194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove"
msgstr "Suprimir"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1196
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removes the selected documentation entry from the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The entry will be removed from the list only. Actual documentation sources "
"remain untouched. You will have to remove them explicitely by other means."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add or change a documentation item"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button to the right of the <guilabel>Location</guilabel> field opens a "
"directory dialog whose entries usually will be filtered according to the "
"file type of the selected configuration page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Title</guilabel> field may not be accessible, depending on the "
"documentation type to be maintained."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: setup.docbook:1224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Documentation List Structure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Every documentation setup page shows the listed documentation items in a "
"table with four columns:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1232
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>TOC</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this check box is marked, this documentation item will show up on the "
"<guilabel>Contents</guilabel> page of the &kdevelop; "
"<guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> facility."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1237
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unchecking the <guilabel>TOC</guilabel> check box will in turn disable the "
"<guilabel>Index</guilabel> and <guilabel>Search</guilabel> check boxes (see "
"below). Thus you cannot have documentation collection items indexed but not "
"shown in the contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1243
#, no-c-format
msgid "Index"
msgstr "Indèx"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this check box is marked, an internal index will be built of this "
"documentation item. This provides fast access to the documentation by the "
"use of the <guilabel>Index</guilabel> and (optionally) <guilabel>Finder</"
"guilabel> pages of the &kdevelop; <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> "
"facility."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The internal index will be built the first time the user selects the "
"<guilabel>Index</guilabel> page. This will delay the first access "
"noticeably, because the index will be read from disk and then cached."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All subsequent indexed searches will however use this chache and thus work "
"significally faster."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search"
msgstr "Recercar"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this check box is marked, the contents of this documentation item will be "
"included in the full text search path of the <guilabel>Search</guilabel> "
"page of the &kdevelop; <guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> facility."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; utilizes the htdig application collection to perform full text "
"searches. This search is done over an internal index, the htdig machinery "
"has to build before it can be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any change of the <guilabel>Search</guilabel> check box marks will thus "
"effect the search runs only after you rebuilt the index on the "
"<guilabel>Search</guilabel> page of the &kdevelop; <guilabel>Documentation</"
"guilabel> facility."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: setup.docbook:1275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Title"
msgstr "Títol"

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the name of the Documentation item as it will be shown on the "
"<guilabel>Contents</guilabel> page of the &kdevelop; "
"<guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> facility."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Former &kdevelop; versions allowed to select the documentation items to be "
"displayed on a per-project basis. This is not available any more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1292
#, no-c-format
msgid "&Qt; Documentation Collections"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1294
#, no-c-format
msgid "On this configuration page all &Qt; documentation is set up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:1303
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Setting up the &Qt; documentation collection</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1304
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Setting up the &Qt; documentation collection</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1310
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally &kdevelop; will fill this in on its first start-up. It looks for "
"standard <filename>*.xml</filename>, or <filename>*.dcf</filename> "
"documentation files in the &Qt; installation directory. The table to the "
"left lists the files &kdevelop; found by their standard titles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a non-standard installation, either there will be no information "
"listed at all or the entries will possibly refer to improper locations (&eg; "
"to another &Qt; installation available in your system). You may adjust the "
"entries using the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-buttons\">buttons</link> to the "
"right of the list field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; will use the titles already provided by the installed &Qt; "
"documentation. Hence the <guilabel>Title</guilabel> field in the "
"<guilabel>Documentation Catalog Properties</guilabel> dialog is inaccessible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, not all &Qt; documentation will be shown on the "
"<guilabel>Contents</guilabel> page of the &kdevelop; "
"<guilabel>Documentation</guilabel> facility. Use the <guilabel>TOC</"
"guilabel> check box in the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-columns\">setup table</"
"link> to select the documentation to be shown."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to have some specific &Qt; documentation included in the search "
"indexes or full text search use the <guilabel>Index</guilabel> and "
"<guilabel>Search</guilabel>check boxes in the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-"
"columns\">setup table</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting Up the CHM Documentation Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this configuration page you may collect documentation according to the "
"&Microsoft; CHM help file standard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:1344
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Setting up &Microsoft; CHM standard documentation files</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1345
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Setting up &Microsoft; CHM standard documentation files</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, this configuration page will be empty (as shown above). You may "
"add new entries using the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-buttons\">buttons</"
"link> to the right of the list field. &kdevelop; will filter <filename>*."
"chm</filename> files in the directory dialog associated to the "
"<guibutton>Add</guibutton> and <guibutton>Edit</guibutton> buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on the format of &Microsoft; <filename>*.chm</filename> "
"files see &eg; PHP: Documentation - Extended CHM Format at <ulink url="
"\"http://de2.php.net/docs-echm.php\">http://de2.php.net/docs-echm.php</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: setup.docbook:1362
#, no-c-format
msgid "Documentation Generated by Doxygen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On this configuration page all &API; documentation generated by &doxygen; is "
"set up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:1373
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Setting up Doxygen generated &API; documentation</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1374
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Setting up Doxygen generated &API; documentation</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In short, such an &API; documents the interface to certain library "
"functions. The &API; documentation on this page should be produced by the "
"externally provided <ulink url=\"http://www.stack.nl/~dimitri/doxygen/"
"\">&doxygen;</ulink> tool."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&doxygen; generated &API; documentationconsists of a series of "
"<filename>html</filename> files, starting with <filename>index.html</"
"filename>. Additionally there may exist <filename>tag</filename> files which "
"contain information to link to already existing &API; documentations. Thus "
"&kdevelop; will look for <filename>index.html</filename> and <filename>*."
"tag</filename> files when seaching for &doxygen; generated &API; "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are some structural constraints assumed when searching for &doxygen; "
"generated &API; documentation. The directory in which the <filename>index."
"html</filename> file resides should contain subdirectories with separate "
"documentation collections. Each of these subdirectories is assumed to "
"contain a <filename>.tag</filename> file and a <filename class=\"directory"
"\">html/</filename> subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1389
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may have a look at <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/"
"share/doc/HTML/en/kdelibs-apidocs</filename> for an example of such a "
"&doxygen; &API; documentation layout."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The older &kde; <ulink url=\"http://sirtaj.net/projects/kdoc/\">KDoc</ulink> "
"generated &API; format is not directly supported any more. If you still want "
"to use such documentation, you may add it on the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-"
"general-custom\">Custom Documentation Collection</link> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; will have filled in a link to the current &kde; Libraries &API;, "
"provided it found one. There are several ways for &kdevelop; to find out:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Either you provided the <command>configure</command> command with the "
"<option>--with-kdelibsdoxy-dir</option> option when you compiled &kdevelop; "
"(see the <link linkend=\"make-api\">How to Obtain a &kdevelop; &API; "
"Documentation</link> chapter)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Or the <command>configure</command> command did automatically find a "
"&doxygen; generated &kde; Libraries &API; in one of several standard "
"locations it knows of."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Or as a last resort the <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/"
"share/doc/HTML/en/kdelibs-apidocs/</filename> was found at the first "
"&kdevelop; startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If &kdevelop; did not find a valid &doxygen; generated &kde; Libraries &API; "
"at its first start-up the <guilabel>Doxygen Documentation Collection</"
"guilabel> list will be empty."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1419
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may add your own &API; documentation entries (&eg; from your current "
"projects) by using the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-buttons\">buttons</link> "
"to the right. If you want to have them included in the indexed and/or full "
"text search mark the <guilabel>Index</guilabel> or <guilabel>Search</"
"guilabel> check boxes in the <link linkend=\"setup-docu-columns\">setup "
"table</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdevelop; uses the title information from the <filename>index.html</"
"filename>. Hence the <guilabel>Title</guilabel> field in the "
"<guilabel>Documentation Catalog Properties</guilabel> dialog is inaccessible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: setup.docbook:1428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; system provides more &API; documentation than the &kde; Libraries "
"&API; only. You will need additional interfaces information if you want to "
"&eg; include the &kate; part into you programs. For this &kate; part &API; "
"for example you should compile and install the &kde; Base Libraries &API; "
"from the <ulink url=\"http://developer.kde.org/source/index.html\">sources</"
"ulink> (using the <command>make apidox</command> and <command>make install</"
"command> commands on the <filename class=\"directory\">kdebase</filename> "
"sources) and then add an entry to the <guilabel>Doxygen Documentation "
"Collection</guilabel> list like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: setup.docbook:1435
